        "definition": "shelter and protection granted by a state to fugitives",
        "definitionCN": "国家对逃难者给予的收留与保护",
        "example": "The court granted her asylum after years of waiting.",
        "exampleCN": "多年等待后，法院给予她庇护。",
        "why": "Greek asylon meant inviolable refuge; the place one cannot be dragged out of.",
        "whyCN": "希腊语 asylon 意为不可侵犯的庇护地——谁也拖不走你的地方。"
      },
      {
        "no": "02",
        "title": "An institution offering shelter or care",
        "titleCN": "收容所；救济院",
        "definition": "an institution giving shelter or care to the needy or ill",
        "definitionCN": "向贫弱或患病者提供收容照料的机构",
        "example": "The old asylum housed orphans until the war.",
        "exampleCN": "那座收容所在战前一直收养孤儿。",
        "why": "The inviolable refuge becomes any safe, enclosed place of care.",
        "whyCN": "「不可侵犯的庇护地」扩展为任何封闭安全的照护之所。"
      }
    ],
    "etymology": {
      "intro": {
        "en": "Asylum comes from Greek asylon, an inviolable place, from a- plus sylon, from sylao, to seize.",
        "cn": "asylum 源自希腊语 asylon（不可侵犯之地），由否定前缀 a- 加 sylon（来自 sylao，抓捕）构成。"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "era": "PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN",
          "en": "The root *sel- meant to take hold.",
          "cn": "词根 *sel- 意为抓取。"
        },
        {
          "era": "GREEK",
          "en": "Sylao meant to plunder; asylon meant beyond seizure.",
          "cn": "希腊语 sylao 意为劫掠；asylon 意为不可被抓之地。"
        },
        {
          "era": "GREEK",
          "en": "Temples and altars served as asyla for fugitives.",
          "cn": "神庙与祭坛曾作逃亡者的庇护所。"
        },
        {
          "era": "LATIN",
          "en": "Latin borrowed asylon as asylum with the same sacred sense.",
          "cn": "拉丁语借用 asylon 为 asylum，仍指神圣庇护地。"
        },
        {
          "era": "ENGLISH, 15TH C.",
          "en": "English took it for sanctuary, later for care institutions and state protection.",
          "cn": "十五世纪英语借入，先指圣所，后指收容机构与国家庇护。"
        }
      ]
    },
